 "relations_about": "The knowledge graph. Relations link concepts to the product attributes that support or weaken them, and say what an attribute can and cannot tell Filo. Relations guide search and explanations; they are never stored as facts about a product. A product fact always needs its own evidence. Numeric thresholds in raises_likelihood and lowers_likelihood (e.g. 200 gsm) are general textile rules of thumb, not sourced findings: use them only to order search candidates, never as a claim to a shopper, and validate them against Filo's own evidence over time.",
 "relation_types": {
  "is_a": "a concept belongs to a broader one (merino is_a wool)",
  "evidenced_by": "product fields that can confirm the concept",
  "raises_likelihood": "makes the concept more likely but never proves it",
  "lowers_likelihood": "makes the concept less likely but never disproves it",
  "depends_on": "other attributes that also decide the outcome",
  "does_not_prove": "a common shortcut Filo must never take",
  "conflicts_with": "cannot both be true for one garment",
  "fit_feature_for": "product features that address a fit concern"
 },
